    "markdown": "![Hugging Face's logo](https://huggingface.co/front/assets/huggingface_logo-noborder.svg) Hugging Face⟨1⟩\n  *  Models ⟨2⟩\n  *  Datasets ⟨3⟩\n  *  Spaces ⟨4⟩\n  *  Buckets new⟨5⟩\n  *  Docs ⟨6⟩\n  *  Enterprise ⟨7⟩\n  * Pricing⟨8⟩\n  *     * Website\n      *  Tasks⟨9⟩\n      *  HuggingChat⟨10⟩\n      *  Collections⟨11⟩\n      *  Languages⟨12⟩\n      *  Organizations⟨13⟩\n    * Community\n      *  Blog⟨14⟩\n      *  Posts⟨15⟩\n      *  Daily Papers⟨16⟩\n      *  Hardware⟨17⟩\n      *  Learn⟨18⟩\n      *  Discord⟨19⟩\n      *  Forum⟨20⟩\n      *  GitHub⟨21⟩\n    * Solutions\n      *  Team & Enterprise⟨7⟩\n      *  Hugging Face PRO⟨22⟩\n      *  Enterprise Support⟨23⟩\n      *  Inference Providers⟨24⟩\n      *  Inference Endpoints⟨25⟩\n      *  Storage Buckets⟨5⟩\n  * * * *\n  * Log In⟨26⟩\n  * Sign Up⟨27⟩\n\n\n# \n ![](https://huggingface.co/avatars/fc1c5e564c58b2769eb8f02dd12f9a22.svg) ⟨28⟩\nProbees1492⟨28⟩\n/\npapersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf⟨29⟩\nlike 0\n Summarization ⟨30⟩ GGUF ⟨31⟩\n5 languages\n llama.cpp ⟨32⟩ qwen2.5 ⟨33⟩ on-device ⟨34⟩ document ⟨35⟩ conversational ⟨36⟩\nLicense: apache-2.0\n Model card ⟨29⟩ Files Files and versions xet ⟨37⟩ Community ⟨38⟩\nDeploy\nCopy to bucket new\nUse this model\n### Instructions to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with libraries, inference providers, notebooks, and local apps. Follow these links to get started.\n  * Libraries\n  *  llama-cpp-python⟨39⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with llama-cpp-python:\n\n```\n# !pip install llama-cpp-python\n\nfrom llama_cpp import Llama\n\nllm = Llama.from_pretrained(\n\trepo_id=\"Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf\",\n\tfilename=\"papersummary-1.5b-v2-q4_k_m.gguf\",\n)\n\n```\n\n```\nllm.create_chat_completion(\n\tmessages = \"\\\"The tower is 324 metres (1,063 ft) tall, about the same height as an 81-storey building, and the tallest structure in Paris. Its base is square, measuring 125 metres (410 ft) on each side. During its construction, the Eiffel Tower surpassed the Washington Monument to become the tallest man-made structure in the world, a title it held for 41 years until the Chrysler Building in New York City was finished in 1930. It was the first structure to reach a height of 300 metres. Due to the addition of a broadcasting aerial at the top of the tower in 1957, it is now taller than the Chrysler Building by 5.2 metres (17 ft). Excluding transmitters, the Eiffel Tower is the second tallest free-standing structure in France after the Millau Viaduct.\\\"\"\n)\n```\n\n  * Notebooks\n  *  Google Colab⟨40⟩\n  *  Kaggle⟨41⟩\n  * Local Apps Settings⟨42⟩\n  *  llama.cpp ⟨43⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with llama.cpp:\n##### Install (macOS, Linux)\n\n```\ncurl -LsSf https://llama.app/install.sh | sh\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\nllama serve -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\nllama cli -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Install from WinGet (Windows)\n\n```\nwinget install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\nllama serve -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\nllama cli -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Use pre-built binary\n\n```\n# Download pre-built binary from:\n# https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp/releases\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n./llama-server -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\n./llama-cli -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Build from source code\n\n```\ngit clone https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp.git\ncd llama.cpp\ncmake -B build\ncmake --build build -j --target llama-server llama-cli\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n./build/bin/llama-server -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n# Run inference directly in the terminal:\n./build/bin/llama-cli -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Use Docker\n\n```\ndocker model run hf.co/Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n  *  LM Studio ⟨44⟩\n  *  Jan ⟨45⟩\n  *  Ollama ⟨46⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with Ollama:\n\n```\nollama run hf.co/Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n  *  Unsloth Studio ⟨47⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with Unsloth Studio:\n##### Install Unsloth Studio (macOS, Linux, WSL)\n\n```\ncurl -fsSL https://unsloth.ai/install.sh | sh\n# Run unsloth studio\nunsloth studio -H 0.0.0.0 -p 8888\n# Then open http://localhost:8888 in your browser\n# Search for Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf to start chatting\n```\n\n##### Install Unsloth Studio (Windows)\n\n```\nirm https://unsloth.ai/install.ps1 | iex\n# Run unsloth studio\nunsloth studio -H 0.0.0.0 -p 8888\n# Then open http://localhost:8888 in your browser\n# Search for Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf to start chatting\n```\n\n##### Using HuggingFace Spaces for Unsloth\n\n```\n# No setup required\n# Open https://huggingface.co/spaces/unsloth/studio in your browser\n# Search for Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf to start chatting\n```\n\n  *  Pi ⟨48⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with Pi:\n##### Start the llama.cpp server\n\n```\n# Install llama.cpp:\nbrew install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server:\nllama serve -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Configure the model in Pi\n\n```\n# Install Pi:\nnpm install -g @mariozechner/pi-coding-agent\n# Add to ~/.pi/agent/models.json:\n{\n  \"providers\": {\n    \"llama-cpp\": {\n      \"baseUrl\": \"http://localhost:8080/v1\",\n      \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n      \"apiKey\": \"none\",\n      \"models\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n##### Run Pi\n\n```\n# Start Pi in your project directory:\npi\n```\n\n  *  Hermes Agent new⟨49⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with Hermes Agent:\n##### Start the llama.cpp server\n\n```\n# Install llama.cpp:\nbrew install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server:\nllama serve -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Configure Hermes\n\n```\n# Install Hermes:\ncurl -fsSL https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/install.sh | bash\nhermes setup\n# Point Hermes at the local server:\nhermes config set model.provider custom\nhermes config set model.base_url http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1\nhermes config set model.default Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Run Hermes\n\n```\nhermes\n```\n\n  *  Atomic Chat new⟨50⟩\n  *  OpenClaw new⟨51⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with OpenClaw:\n##### Start the llama.cpp server\n\n```\n# Install llama.cpp:\nbrew install llama.cpp\n# Start a local OpenAI-compatible server:\nllama serve -hf Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Configure OpenClaw\n\n```\n# Install OpenClaw:\nnpm install -g openclaw@latest\n# Register the local server and set it as the default model:\nopenclaw onboard --non-interactive --mode local \\\n  --auth-choice custom-api-key \\\n  --custom-base-url http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1 \\\n  --custom-model-id \"Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\" \\\n  --custom-provider-id llama-cpp \\\n  --custom-compatibility openai \\\n  --custom-text-input \\\n  --accept-risk \\\n  --skip-health\n```\n\n##### Run OpenClaw\n\n```\nopenclaw agent --local --agent main --message \"Hello from Hugging Face\"\n```\n\n  *  Docker Model Runner ⟨52⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with Docker Model Runner:\n\n```\ndocker model run hf.co/Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n  *  Lemonade ⟨53⟩\nHow to use Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf with Lemonade:\n##### Pull the model\n\n```\n# Download Lemonade from https://lemonade-server.ai/\nlemonade pull Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf:Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### Run and chat with the model\n\n```\nlemonade run user.papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf-Q4_K_M\n```\n\n##### List all available models\n\n```\nlemonade list\n```\n\n\n\n  * PaperSummary 1.5B (fine-tuned, Q4_K_M GGUF)⟨54⟩\n\n\n#   ⟨55⟩ PaperSummary 1.5B (fine-tuned, Q4_K_M GGUF) \nOn-device document-summarization engine for the **PaperSummary** app. A supervised fine-tune (LoRA) of **Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct** , distilled from Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct, aligned to the app output contract: structured `Title / Description / Summary` markers, faithful markdown, level/format control, 29 languages, and map-reduce merge for long documents.\n  * **Format** : GGUF, **Q4_K_M** (runs via llama.cpp / llama.rn, Metal/GPU), n_ctx 4096\n  * **File** : `papersummary-1.5b-v2-q4_k_m.gguf` (986,048,000 bytes)\n  * **Improvements over stock Qwen2.5-1.5B** (measured): output-marker compliance 71%→100%, cross-lingual output language obeyed, map-reduce merge without hallucinated figures.\n  * **License** : Apache-2.0 (inherits Qwen2.5). Fine-tune data generated synthetically.\n\n\nIntended as a drop-in engine download for the app; not a general chat model. \n\nDownloads last month\n    69\nGGUF⟨56⟩\nModel size\n2B params\nArchitecture\nqwen2\nChat template\nHardware compatibility\nLog In⟨57⟩ to add your hardware\n4-bit\nQ4_K_M 986 MB\nInference Providers NEW⟨58⟩\n Summarization ⟨59⟩\nThis model isn't deployed by any Inference Provider. 🙋 Ask for provider support⟨60⟩\n##  Model tree for Probees1492/papersummary-1.5b-v2-gguf ⟨61⟩\nBase model\nQwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B⟨62⟩\nFinetuned\nQwen/Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct⟨63⟩\nQuantized\n(237⟨64⟩)\nthis model\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨65⟩ Privacy⟨66⟩ About⟨67⟩ Careers⟨68⟩ ⟨1⟩\nWebsite\nModels⟨2⟩ Datasets⟨3⟩ Spaces⟨4⟩ Pricing⟨8⟩ Docs⟨6⟩\nInference providers allow you to run inference using different serverless providers.\n",
